Description: Build exr at opt-level 1, for reproducibility on arm64
 emeraldian intermittently fails to reproduce on arm64. LLVM compiles exr's
 DWA decoder (exr::compression::dwa::lossy_dct::decode_lossy_channels)
 non-deterministically: two builds of the same source can assign x10 and x11
 the other way round across four instructions with identical semantics. zola
 0.23.6-4 works around the same function the same way. exr arrives through
 ratatui-image's image-defaults feature, and debian/rules asserts it is still
 in Cargo.lock.
 .
 A workaround, not a repair: drop it once LLVM fixes the non-determinism,
 confirmed over several builds on arm64.
Author: pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-28
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -57,6 +57,11 @@
 strip = true
 opt-level = 3
 
+# See debian/patches/deoptimise-exr-for-reproducibility.patch: LLVM compiles
+# exr's DWA decoder non-deterministically on arm64.
+[profile.release.package.exr]
+opt-level = 1
+
 # Dependencies are slow to compile but hot in the render loop; optimize them
 # even in debug builds so `cargo run` is still smooth at 60fps.
 [profile.dev.package."*"]
